course: dictionary
lesson: 13109
title: Flattened and its many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Flattened» comes from the word «flatten», which means to make something flat. It is the past form, so it tells you the flattening has already happened.
explain: «The baker flattened the dough with a rolling pin.» The pin pressed the dough until it was flat. Now check your meaning: put «made flat» in place of «flattened» and see if the sentence still makes sense. It does.
explain: «The storm flattened the trees.» Here flatten means knocked down to the ground. The trees did not get thinner. They fell over. Context tells you which meaning fits.
fact: Flatten means to make something flat, or to knock something down to the ground.
fact: «Flattened» is the past form of «flatten»: flatten, flattens, flattened, flattening.
fact: «Flattened» can also describe a shape, as in «a flattened ball».
fact: The Earth is slightly flattened at the poles, the top and bottom of the globe.
fact: Scientists say a flattened shape can show pressure or force pushing on an object.
exercise: «The storm flattened the tall trees in the park.» What does flattened mean here? | *Knocked down to the ground | Painted bright green | Lifted high into the sky | Counted one by one
exercise: Which word is the past form of flatten? | flatten | *flattened | flattens | flattening
exercise: «The baker flattened the dough with a rolling pin.» What was made flat? | The kitchen table | The rolling pin | *The dough | The baker
test: In «a flattened ball», what does flattened tell you? | The ball is very heavy | *The ball has a flat shape | The ball's colour | The ball makes a loud noise
test: Which sentence shows flatten meaning knocked down? | The paper was flattened under a heavy book. | *The gale flattened the fence overnight. | The chef flattened the pizza base. | The pancake was flattened with a spatula.
exam: Which word means made flat by pressing or squashing? | Counted | Lifted | *Flattened | Painted
